{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for Lending Draft4 at exact 8daef24750062df072ea3da233ae2b894a407fd1, primary7eb9c31912b81b35033e0647ee2d3318c32fddc5 FIRST, normally assigned original64423d28/b41311f5. Design only. The native declaration and complete demo are feasible; one P2 browser recovery requirement is missing.\n\nP2 — Retain the original lending act and the separate publication workflow before dispatch (§4,§6,§9). Keeping a device key does not retain a signed donation. If a donation is accepted but its reply is lost, signing a fresh donation after reload can open another thing; state alone cannot uniquely identify the original request. Likewise the existing one-file editor is not an automatic recovery mechanism: commands1517–1529 explicitly warns that a fresh propose/edit creates another lane/signs new requests and does not retain the uncertain request's original envelope.\n\nRequire durable target/full incarnation, signer, operation identity/deadline, signed envelope and needed private inputs before submitting each lending act. After unknown outcome/reload, offer read-only Check/settlement of that original and explicit continuation, never silent replacement or duplicate donation. Retain the accepted lending fact separately from publication status. For publication, retain original page bytes/base and coherent source snapshot, lane/repository refs, edit-stage keys/envelopes and learned receipts before each mutation; recover the same lane/stages after lost replies. Show lending accepted separately from shelf pending/refused/unknown/published. A refused lending act must not manufacture a state change or be called published.\n\nAdd prospective acceptance cases for lost replies/reloads during donation and each open/propose/merge stage: one original thing/intent/lane, no replacement key/envelope, exact receipt and actionable status. An explicit Refresh from newly confirmed state is NEW authorized work and may open another lane; distinguish it from retrying an unknown original. Confirmed abandonment/new work remains allowed. Keep the acknowledged stale/manual-copy boundary; do not require atomic fold publication or guarantee success across permanent failures.\n\nNative feasibility is credited: restricted profile, trusted opener injection at genesis, activated definition/dependency closure,64 live things excluding final gone, immutable name/description, optional borrower clearing, member return without borrower-only guard, and staff cancellation with attributed text. Use canonical empty genesis values when opener is the only supplied field. Staff is a library responsibility using an existing native role, not a new native membership role. set-actions replaces a role's whole list; preserve existing administration/application/change actions when adding lending grants.\n\nCohort facts: the specified application cohort is Register5/Directory5/Membership4/Rules3/Destination2. Existing CLI maps/readers/invites and the legacy one-file edit path can support it; the conditional Destination3 manifest-list path is not its default. D7 lacks the application factory and must not silently replace this cohort. Name the compatible activated legacy change and cohort-correct browser joining in the runbook/build: current Page admission for membership1/2 is not proof of membership4 browser parity. These remain prospective real-service witnesses, not a new protocol rule or a proved cohort blocker.\n\nSecurity and provenance criteria: serialize donated names/descriptions/reasons as literal text, so Markdown headings/links/newlines cannot forge generated Status/Record lines. Existing native renderer safety was inspected; no existing XSS is alleged. Use the canonical numeric Item ID for shelf paths, never a user's name. Capture state and its full scope/incarnation/seq/hash coherently for the Record pointer. Fence stale callbacks/room changes and visibly identify behind projections. Refresh must include gone items/reasons and complete paging, not just the64 live summary. The public folder lists titles for its first100 Markdown files and filenames thereafter; lifetime cancelled pages can exceed100, so qualify unlimited-title claims.\n\nP3 visitor clarity: public shelf/published thing or commit history can meet the visitor outcome while the authoritative native journal remains seat-protected. State which history an unseated visitor sees and label the member-only record link. Do not invent anonymous native permissions or infer this from standalone Counter behavior.\n\nArchitecture: one authoritative lending scope plus a repairable repository/site projection is appropriate, with original operation custody across the two separate writes. Security: native grants remain authority, independent participant keys and exact scope binding remain necessary. Simplification: keep five acts, one page per thing and one compatible editor; publication-from-fold remains separately deferred, not a prerequisite.\n\nPreserve the full story: all nine steps, non-act small-pot offer, exact short Baby description, supplied spoken line only in the recording, staff's attributed cancellation reason, and both explicit refusals. Preserve all seven browser requirements and all six§9 outputs: canonical declaration/pin and real-scope scenario/refusals, browser, executed deployed runbook, recording script, online room with story already played, and homepage library page with room/library/counter/jam/documentation order. Add another-member return, capacity/final-state and role-preservation witnesses without replacing the story. No schedule estimate or15:00 boundary narrows functionality.\n\nCoverage: Root primary FIRST direct FULL14701B298LF SHA833ec175e73b284fcbce824993b3a2bf808f41bc9805636d01058efcb6172b6b in four bounded spans/EOF. Three peer reports FULL and cohort correction addenda; native application module FULL, other support selected FULL/whole PARTIAL with exact baseline562/current062 equality. Root separately read log/verify, existing editor's lost-reply warning and actual cohort maps. The earlier conditional Destination3 interpretation was checked and corrected; no unsupported-CLI claim adopted. No Source execution/validation/tests/gate/build/install/browser/provider/private reads or Source edits. Every proposed witness, deployed publication and final online acceptance remains unrun. Logo priority interruption was honored before filing this resumed review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7eb9c31912b81b35033e0647ee2d3318c32fddc5","binding":"assigned","head":"8daef24750062df072ea3da233ae2b894a407fd1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0c203045fdd38ac95bc526e546c721fe35b516a5\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b9dd0ef2612cd06dc79fdbd704b3108678a7bff\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b41311f5fc55bb2ac6de2b36a1941e717b0f92d5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f44672b3f76e5ed031e597aaa101349f20950f9e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}